# implements-port slice 13: -1 does not fit size_t, so the root's edge (row int -> size_t, receiver
# lm_stg_convert_int_size_t) refuses; the receiver's `range` is the root's own `convert` (the call's
# catch rows renumber every status the receiver leaves with, l2_rw_catch_edge), uncaught: R0
# stops with status 3 and sends no exit.  Mutant: the rows not written -- the walk notes the
# receiver's own 1.
size_t: s 0U
int: x -1
s: x
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
